From d7e31deedb8bfa8872628f93e503814a5a69edbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:04:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The cameraman keeps the crew in the picture, has a wide shot,
 and stays on the fight through a setup's teleports (patch 0090)

Three faults from filming the rebuilt Deadmines bosses with `WOW_SPECTATE` (patches 0088, 0089) on
Nov 9:

- No shot ever showed Gilnid's engineers on their planks, 8.6 and 9.7 yd over the pit. The spec
  takes a crew now, `<subject>,<hero>,<shot>,<crew>|<crew>`: each living one within 15 yd of the
  subject or the hero (along the ground, so overhead counts) is kept in the picture with the two,
  from every shot: the camera looks at the middle of them all, feet to heads, and stands back (to
  50 yd) until every one fits; a position where the world hides one scores worse.
- A `wide` shot: 20 to 25 yd out and 30 degrees up, for the arena (the crew on their planks, the
  valve's fire stripe across the pit). `high` was too close and too steep in the Foundry (whole
  stretches of bare orange floor): 15 to 22 yd at 45 degrees, from 12 to 18 at 52. Under a low
  roof (the Foundry's cave) every shot's positions are tried 12 and 24 degrees lower before the
  eye comes in along its line, so a wide shot stays wide.
- A clip cut to 5 s, and the camera on the wrong spot (or frozen, or inside a rock) for the
  video's first seconds. The hero fell in a setup (pirates at the landing), was teleported and
  healed before the video, and the camera held where he fell. A teleport is now the hero 15 yd
  or more away within half a second (a remote mover glides there over a few frames), taken once
  they've landed: the camera picks its position afresh there, straight away, and for 2.5 s after
  looks again every quarter second as the world there loads in; until a position is free it waits
  6 yd from the fight, not inside a rock that isn't solid yet. An eye with the world between it and
  both of the two (seen from them) for 0.3 s is a cut. A fight over is on again at once when the
  hero, up, is moved beside a living subject 3 s or more after the fall (sooner is a fallen hero
  sent to a lamp, which still holds). The hero falls only once down for 0.3 s. (The rig, in Basin
  Battle, ends the video only on a fall after the video started.)
